    "content" : "Proof. Let L, r, and p0 be as in the statement of the lemma. We may assume that p0 = p− is the south pole. Let ψ be the stereographic projection based at the north pole p+ and let ϱ be its inverse. Set r1 arccot(L) and let κ denote the biLipschitz constant of the restriction of ψ to S2 \\ B(p+,r1). Finally, set r0 2−1 · min{r1, L−1,κ−2}."
